  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Western New England University is a private, non-profit university in Springfield, Massachusetts. Founded in 1919 as the Springfield Division of Northeastern College, it gained independent college status in 1951 and became a university in 2011. The 215-acre suburban campus is home to about 3,700 students across five colleges: Arts and Sciences, Business, Engineering, Pharmacy and Health Sciences, and the School of Law.",
      "WNE is best known for its tight-knit professional schools — the only law school in Western Massachusetts, an accredited Doctor of Pharmacy programme, and an ABET-accredited College of Engineering offering biomedical, civil, computer, electrical, industrial, and mechanical engineering. The 0-6 PharmD and 3+3 Doctor of Occupational Therapy programmes let undergraduates progress directly into doctoral training.",
      "Springfield, MA gives students access to a mid-sized New England city with strong industry ties — 39 km from Bradley International Airport, 138 km from Boston, and 241 km from New York City. International students make up about 5% of the student body, drawn from 30 countries.",
      "Combined and dual-degree pathways are a WNE signature: Engineering/Law (6 years), JD/MBA, PharmD/MBA, OTD/MBA, five-year BS/MS engineering tracks, and five-year Bachelor/MBA programmes give students faster, integrated routes to advanced credentials."
    ],
